Author: gal-engines <gal@local>
Date:   Sun Oct 25 12:27:36 2026 +0800

    gal: a game missing its data files is not a pass
    
    The verdict only looked for engine failures, so a game whose files are absent sailed
    through: the lifegame demo has been reported as runnable all along while asking for five
    cursor bitmaps it does not ship.  Carrying on without them is the engine being tolerant,
    not the game working, so 'can't find file', '*** can't', 'no decoder' and 'invalid' now
    count against it.
    
    lifegame consequently reads as failing - honestly, until its data is complete.

diff --git a/gal b/gal
index 2031b9d..2d3d58b 100755
--- a/gal
+++ b/gal
@@ -1007,9 +1007,13 @@ def cmd_verify(args):
     # Survival is not a compatibility test.  Catch explicit engine/script
     # failures (including KiriKiri's Japanese exception banner) even when the
     # host keeps its run loop alive or exits with status zero.
+    # A missing data file is a failure too: the engine may carry on without it, but
+    # the game is not running the way its author meant.  The cursor files some NScripter
+    # demos leave out are the common case.
     error_markers = (
-        "error", "can't open font", "krkrrun:",
-        "エラーが発生しました", "does not exist", "exception",
+        "error", "can't open font", "can't find file", "krkrrun:",
+        "エラーが発生しました", "does not exist", "exception", "*** can't",
+        "no decoder", "invalid",
     )
     errors = [l for l in lines if any(m in l.lower() for m in error_markers)]
     if proc.returncode not in (None, 0) and not timed_out:
